 "text": "Hey there, how are you? Not rude at all. typical in fast food places. They expect it. Saves them coming around with the bill. Splitting the bill is fine, too. Just say before you order, so they can make sure enough food for everyone. A couple of dollars per person is about right. More for the busier places that have to keep the lights on whether the place is busy or not. You' welcome. Tipping is about fast food as much as it is for cafes and restaurants. The rules are pretty much the same.",
